From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: cpuidle: psci: register Exynos 7870 deep states switched off (J701F local)

Written by Claude 2026-10-10 for the J701F project; not an upstream patch.
The PSCI core power-down state added by exynos7870-j7velte-cpuidle.dts is
untested firmware territory. With CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF a boot never enters it; a
core is opted in at run time through sysfs, so a hang cannot become a boot loop.
---
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -409,6 +409,18 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * J701F local: on Exynos 7870 the deep states are an experiment. Register
+	 * them switched off; they are enabled per core through
+	 * /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpuN/cpuidle/stateM/disable.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,exynos7870")) {
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 1; i < drv->state_count; i++)
+			drv->states[i].flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF;
+	}
+
 	ret = cpuidle_register(drv, NULL);
 	if (ret)
 		goto deinit;
